A formal register of communication used to express politeness and respect. In Ukrainian, this applies to the second-person singular pronoun ‘Ви’ (capitalised in personal correspondence), which formally coincides with the second-person plural pronoun ‘ви’, but functions as a polite form of address to one person.
The formal ‘Ви’ is morphologically identical to the second-person plural pronoun, so the feature ‘Polite=Form’ is used to distinguish between them. 
In informal communication, the pronoun ‘ти’ (you-singular-informal) is used, which is not marked with the feature ‘Polite’.

### <a name="Form">`Form`</a>: formal register

#### Examples

* [uk] _<b>Дякую вам, пане!</b>_ “Thank you, sir!”
